# Who is asked to review what.
#
# GitHub reads this file to assign reviewers automatically. It is *advisory*
# until branch protection on `main` turns on "Require review from Code Owners";
# without that setting a pull request can still be merged with nobody named
# here having looked at it. Adding the file and enabling the rule are two
# separate decisions, and only the first is made by committing this.
#
# One caveat worth knowing before enabling the rule: GitHub does not let an
# author approve their own pull request. With a single code owner, turning on
# "Require review from Code Owners" means every pull request that owner opens
# needs either a second reviewer or an admin override. That is a reason to add
# a second owner, not a reason to skip the file.

# Everything, by default.
* @pixie79

# The paths below are already covered by the rule above. They are named
# individually so that the day a team is added as a broad owner — which is the
# usual way a repository grows — these do not quietly move with it. Each is
# something where a wrong merge is expensive or irreversible.

# Publishing. `cargo publish` cannot be undone: a version can be yanked but
# never deleted, and the number is burned for good.
/.github/workflows/release.yml   @pixie79
/docs/PUBLISHING.md              @pixie79
/tools/publish-order.py          @pixie79

# The provenance record, and the bytes it vouches for. This repository exists
# because a vendored schema once had no version, no source URL and no fetch
# date; an unreviewed edit here is that defect returning.
/specs.toml                      @pixie79
/schemas/                        @pixie79

# The gates. Weakening one of these is how a rule stops being enforced without
# anybody deciding that it should.
/deny.toml                       @pixie79
/clippy.toml                     @pixie79
/.github/workflows/ci.yml        @pixie79

# Licensing. Every crate declares `MIT OR Apache-2.0` and ships these texts by
# symbolic link, so a change here changes the terms in every published tarball.
/LICENSE-MIT                     @pixie79
/LICENSE-APACHE                  @pixie79
